# Binary
cali-go-stack
tmp/
/gogogo

# The repo tracks its own helper scripts under bin/ (check-*.sh, datastar-lint,
# init-secrets, setup-hooks.sh). A global ~/.gitignore_global commonly ignores
# `bin/`, and that rule silently wins over `git add` — a script referenced by
# .lefthook.yml once failed to be committed because of it, leaving the hook
# pointing at a file that did not exist in the repo.
#
# `git add -f` works but depends on remembering every time. These negations
# un-ignore the directory for this repo, so the normal `git add` path is
# correct by default. Nothing else belongs in bin/ at the root.
!bin/
!bin/**

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Go
vendor/

# Data
data/

# Build
dist/

# Agent / hidden tooling artifacts (never commit; keep CI config under .github/)
# Any directory starting with a dot is ignored, except .github/ (workflows).
.pi-subagents/
.*/
!.github/
!.githooks/
# Cali agent workflow artifacts (execution critiques, UX audits, etc)
.cali-*/

# Test/binary data artifacts
internal/workflow/pb_data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Node.js (Tailwind v4 + DaisyUI v5 build)
node_modules/

# Web resources (hand-rolled CSS, kept committed)

# Root-level logo is a social-card asset (1024px), not for the README — see web/resources/static/logo.png
/logo.png
/app
/gogogo
coverage.html
coverage.out

# Generated draft posts (CONTENT_WRITING.md stays tracked; posts/ do not)
posts/

# stelow skill artifacts
stelow.json

# Pre-built binaries (belong in releases, not in the repo)
gogogo-desktop
gogogo-gui
# A bare `go build ./cmd/<x>/` drops a binary named after the package at the
# repo root. `go run` (what the Makefile targets use) never does.
/check-skill-frontmatter
/check-scope
# cmd/gogogo-mcp is its OWN module, so building it from inside that directory
# drops the binary THERE, not at the root — and the root-level rules above do
# not match. Caught a 12MB artifact staged into a commit once.
/cmd/gogogo-mcp/gogogo-mcp
# Any other stray build output in a cmd/ package dir (same reason, defers to
# the explicit entries above for the ones already named).
/cmd/*/gogogo
# `make desktop` (wails3) drops an untagged binary named after the app at the
# repo root; ignore it by exact path so a `desktop/` source dir would be safe.
/desktop

# Investigation spikes (local only, never commit).
#
# IMPORTANT: keep a go.mod inside spikes/ (also gitignored) so the directory is
# its own module. Without it, spikes/ is part of the main module on any machine
# that has it checked out, and a spike importing a package the app does not use
# promotes that package to a DIRECT requirement of the app's go.mod. Since CI
# never sees spikes/, `go mod tidy` then disagrees between local and CI and the
# pre-commit mod-tidy hook can never pass. Minimal contents:
#
#     module spikes
#     go 1.27
spikes/

# Python tooling artifacts (migrate-scope.py and check-scope checks the
# tree, but the bytecode cache never belongs in the repo).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Docs site (site/) -----------------------------------------------------
# Sources are versioned: docs/*.md, site/index.html, site/styles.css,
# site/build.mjs, site/assets/. The RENDERED output is generated by
# `node site/build.mjs` (and rebuilt in CI by .github/workflows/pages.yml),
# so it must never be committed — a stale committed copy would silently
# diverge from the markdown and get published.
site/docs/
site/releases/
site/llms.txt
site/llms-full.txt
site/sitemap.xml

# Autoresearch session state (branch-local, never committed)
.auto/
